<title>UK: Southampton shares up on return to market.</title>
<headline>Southampton shares up on return to market.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Secure Retirement Plc rose 95-1/2p to 142-1/2p by 0915 GMT on Tuesday on their return to the market after a reverse takeover by Southampton Football Club.</p>
<p>The shares, still known by the former name, were suspended pending the takeover last month and last traded at 47p.</p>
<p>The reverse takeover gave Southampton FC access to a stock market listing at a time when an increasing number of football clubs are coming to the market. Other clubs planning to list include Newcastle and Birmingham City.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom, +44 171 542 7945</p>
